EVALUATION.md §7.1: dereferencing a ref to a missing key is a hard E3501 in the reader
(verify reports the ref itself, soft, in stage B). The keys of a keyed list are dynamic
(TYPES.md §4.1), so the symbolic key zz reaches evaluation.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// R.
record R {
  /// K.
  k: String
  /// X.
  x: Int
}

/// Rs.
let rs: [R] keyed by k = [R { k: "a", x: 1 }]

/// P.
let p: ref rs = zz

/// V.
let v: Int = p.x
-- findings.txt --
error[E3501]  a/a.canon:16:17
  p: unknown key zz in rs
  expected by a/a.canon:16 (p: ref rs)

error[E3501]  a/a.canon:19:14
  unknown key zz in rs

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
